#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# r_solve_value

#% text
# `r_solve_value(eqs, a(n), n)` gives the solution of a linear recurrence as an expression in `n`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It solves as `r_solve` does.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Tripling from 2:

#% cell
r_solve_value([a(n) == 3*a(n - 1), a(0) == 2], a(n), n)
#% output
#= 2*3^n

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The general solution:

#% cell
r_solve_value(a(n + 2) == a(n), a(n), n)
#% output
#= c(2) + c(1)*(-1)^n

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `r_solve` gives rules:

#% cell
r_solve([a(n) == 3*a(n - 1), a(0) == 2], a(n), n)
#% output
#= [[a(n) -> 2*3^n]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `r_solve`, `d_solve_value`
